WEBVTT

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.230
Royal straight flush.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.570
They stink!

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.370
What the hell are these things?!

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:29.670
<b>Episode 2  "Cloud Mirror"</b>

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.320
They are yaks.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.960
Even-toed ungulates from 
order Artiodactyla, family Bovidae.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.000
They are used for riding, 
their hides, and even for food.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:38.100
I wasn't asking for trivia.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.370
But isn't it great how warm these guys are?

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.020
It gets really cold around here at night.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:47.110
If I wanted warmth, 
I'd prefer to get it from a hottie,

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.020
and if I'm going to sleep, I'd prefer a bed.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.430
Quit your damn complaining, 
you wuss of a water sprite.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.770
Just go back to sleep 
and never wake up again.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:57.940
Sanzo-sama...

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:01.690
I don't have a single cigarette to give you.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.340
Tch, it's not like you'd be losing anything.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.820
Yes, I would.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:08.950
Took you long enough!

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.410
<i>We went out like we were going to buy 
some smokes, and ended up on a journey.</i>

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:50.210
Apparently there's nothing 
but mountains around here.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:53.270
We're going to be enjoying this 
scenery for quite some time.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.510
India, huh? How much farther is it?

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.770
I'm not exactly sure...

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.030
But we are definitely getting closer.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.530
We're encountering demons 
more frequently, too.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.940
Because of Lady Gyokumen's 
Gyumaou resurrection experiment,

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:14.170
a negative aura has spread from 
the west, turning the lands to ruins

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:19.050
and causing the demons to 
lose control of themselves.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.430
Perhaps it could be out of fear
 of being attacked by demons,

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.600
but the villages around here 
seem rather closed off.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.330
They probably don't have any other choice

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.820
in order to survive.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.850
I have a hard time believing that even if we

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.900
storm into Houtou Castle, defeat the end boss and stop the experiment

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.820
that everything will be solved 
and things will go back to normal.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.310
Do you want to step out the car then?

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.190
You can't be serious.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.580
Well, you can basically say that 
we're stuck with each other.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.700
If I had a choice, I'd rather be stuck 
with some hotties than some guys.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.600
Shut up. I'll kill you.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.680
Man, I'm so hungry! I'm so thirsty!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.590
Shut up, you stupid monkey.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.340
Why'd you have to go and ruin 
the serious atmosphere?

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.790
But it's true we're out of water and cigarettes,

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.110
so if we don't stop somewhere soon,
 we're gonna shrivel up.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.190
There should be a village 
just a bit further ahead.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.890
Stop screaming in my ear!

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.100
I was finally—

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.620
Hey, look over there!

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.370
According to this map, it's a lake.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.500
Let's go get some water before 
we head into the village.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.380
What's the matter?

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.710
Man, that's salty. What the heck?

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:47.810
This must be a salt lake.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.220
And a highly concentrated one at that.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.720
A salt lake... So a lake filled with salt water.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.100
With such a high concentration of salt,

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.230
I'm pretty sure we could float 
rather easily, without even trying.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.160
What do you mean? Our bodies would float?

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:08.270
A higher salt concentration in the water
 results in a lower specific gravity.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:11.420
That makes it easier for things to float.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.510
Great, so we can float in it, 
but still can't drink it.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:18.630
But it's so pretty.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.920
What are you doing there?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.930
Are you humans?

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.470
Well, I am, at least.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:35.090
But I'm not so sure about those guys.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:35.810
What?!

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:36.680
Wha...

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:37.570
Demons?

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:41.310
We've found you, Sanzo party of outlaws!

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.800
It's the same line every damn time.
 We're seriously getting sick of it.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.400
The lack of vocabulary among demons 
is a rather alarming problem.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.510
Oh, right. I'm out of cigarettes.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:13.500
I'm even more hungry now 
that we moved around.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.360
Are you...

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.510
really human?

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:23.010
Thanks to that lake,

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:27.780
we've grown rather prosperous from 
producing and distributing salt.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.350
As you can see, there are a lot 
of people in our village,

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.530
so the demons don't attack directly.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:39.600
But lately, they come down from the 
mountains to steal the salt we go out to sell,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.470
or attack our transport wagons.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.800
Who are you?

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.310
They're apparently travelers...

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.180
They saved us from...

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.430
I see.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.680
So you're a priest traveling west...

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.390
It's true that our villagers have been 
attacked by demons numerous times

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.680
and we've suffered major 
losses because of them.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.490
If you're able to exterminate them,

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.930
I wouldn't mind giving you lodging 
and supplies for your journey.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:13.450
Wait, why are you acting all high and mighty?

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:18.410
We only came here because he said he'd 
take care of us as thanks for saving him.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:19.760
Yes, but...

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.320
You got a problem?

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:26.030
Our village can't live in peace 
because of those demons.

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:29.830
If there's something you want, we're going
 to have to ask for something in return.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.710
We're not experts in demon 
extermination or anything.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.790
Let's go.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.220
Very well. We accept.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.440
Huh?!

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.690
Who died and made you king?!

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.390
If you want some food, just use 
the damn credit card to buy some.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:50.020
Apparently that card won't 
work in this remote area.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.530
What?

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:54.880
I peered into some nearby shops earlier,

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:57.900
but there wasn't a single shop 
that would take cards.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:00.710
We're almost completely out of cash as well.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:02.690
Then what about food?

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.160
We'll have to wait.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:04.840
And cigarettes?

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:05.660
No.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.380
Oh, come on! A smoke wouldn't hurt!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.800
Moving forward, if we're 
unable to use our card,

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.920
I would like to refrain from 
spending any unnecessary funds.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:15.220
But cigarettes aren't unnecessary!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.730
If you want something 
to chew on, I have some gum.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.510
So what will it be?

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:21.610
Are you going to do it or not?

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.540
I'm sorry we're asking for 
help in such an awful way.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.600
You need to train him better.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.690
It's out of our hands.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:36.030
The influence of the great Sanzo
 apparently doesn't reach this far.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:40.710
If we don't have any cigarettes or food,
 we don't have much of a choice.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.380
Now that that's settled, 
let's hurry up and go!

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.060
And then find some restaurant...

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:46.050
Please wait.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:52.110
The demons will be waiting for us 
to ship out our specialty salt.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:56.840
We'd like for all of you to guard the wagon.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.180
And where's the wagon?

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.590
It'll be leaving this afternoon.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:05.030
Once I'm done loading it, 
I'll give you a call, so until then...

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:06.100
What?

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.760
I guess it can't be helped.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.560
Then we can discuss the reward
 for our services until then.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:14.670
Yeah, I'm gonna leave that 
troublesome crap to you.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:17.070
I'm gonna go wander around.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.060
Me, too!

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.450
Prepare a room. And a bed.

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:25.440
You slept all that time on Hakuryu 
and you still didn't get enough sleep?

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.780
They do say that kids who get 
plenty of sleep mature faster.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:28.960
Mature?

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.340
If he matures any more,
 he's just going to go bald.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.850
I'll kill you, you shitty water sprite.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:36.360
All right, all right. You're free 
to sleep or wander around.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.960
Just be back by the time 
we're supposed to leave.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:39.840
Okay!

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.090
How old are you, five?!

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:49.880
Gramps, is there a tobacco shop nearby?

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:54.970
Are you a traveler? I don't think I've seen 
clothes like that around here before.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:55.370
Yeah.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.870
There's a tobacco shop just up ahead.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:00.610
Thanks.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:03.360
That's an unusual cigarette. 
What's the brand?

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.620
It's locally made.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:08.500
You want to try one?

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:10.720
Thanks.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.950
Okay, here I go!

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.970
Oh, sorry. Did I scare you?

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.520
N-No...

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.350
Whatcha playin'? Can I play, too?

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:35.680
Okay, come play with us.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.200
How do you play?

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.440
This is our territory, and...

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.710
Um... I'm terribly sorry to wake you.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.750
Please, use this if you'd like.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:56.820
Thanks.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.730
Where did all of you come from?

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:04.690
From a city in the east called Chang'an.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.650
Chang'an...

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:15.310
You can look, but don't touch.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:19.860
I heard that you're going 
to protect the wagon.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:26.100
I heard that you're going to 
exterminate the demons for us. I...

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:34.700
Well, it's not a Hi-lite, but...

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.670
Oh, well.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:49.170
<i>Damn, she's hot.</i>

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.830
<i>Uh oh...</i>

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.330
Um, is something wrong?

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:05.150
Huh? Oh, it's nothing.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:06.640
Don't mind me.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:07.370
But...

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:10.700
Well, you see, my cigarette...

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.360
Cigarette?

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:13.820
It's fine. Don't worry about it. 
You just go on ahead.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.240
If you need cigarettes, 
I run a tobacco shop.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:20.990
Oh, I see. Yeah, got it.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.000
I promise to stop by later.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:28.660
Could you do me a favor and just
 wait for me at the shop for now?

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:29.510
But...

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.810
Isn't something the matter?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.300
The matter, huh?

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.100
So good!

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.570
Are they that good?

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.330
Yeah! They're great!

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:44.820
Can I have one more?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.280
Sure. My kids are tired of eating them,

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.870
so eat as many as you'd like.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:53.800
It's always the same thing. 
They're so dry and gross.

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:54.590
Hush up.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.130
Sorry about this.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:13:00.090
Not only did you let me play with you 
guys, now you're feeding me, too.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.470
Well considering how loud your stomach 
rumbled, we had to do something.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:06.960
Are they all your kids?

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.960
Well, actually...

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:15.800
There are a lot of kids in this village who 
lost their parents to the demon attacks,

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.570
so I took them in and care for them.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.840
I see...

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.030
Um...

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.280
What's your name?

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.020
It's Goku.

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:32.100
Okay, Goku-niichan.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.180
They don't seem to be coming back...

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:08.550
Kou!

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:10.050
Kou!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.440
Mother...

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:17.420
Kou, there you are.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:19.930
Dokugaku.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:24.420
Sorry to bother you, but 
Lady Gyokumen is looking for you.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.260
All right.

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:34.670
Ni Jianyi disappeared?

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:40.190
The resurrection experiment
 will stall until his return,

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:45.670
but either way, we still don't have all of 
the Founding Scriptures of Heaven and Earth.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:52.700
I need you to hurry up and obtain
 the other scriptures for me.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:59.770
Wait. Our priority should be the
 Maten Scripture that Genjo Sanzo has.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:08.220
If more demons are just going to die trying 
to get the bounty on his head, then I'll...

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:12.970
Oh, my... Considering the number of times 
you've come back utterly defeated,

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.060
are you one to talk, little boy?

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:21.800
It looks like your friends 
didn't show up after all.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:25.940
I can imagine why one of 
them didn't show up.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.380
But the other two...

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:34.110
Well, I'm pretty sure 
I can handle this myself.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:40.650
I'm counting on you. This salt is 
an important part of our livelihood.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:47.610
Many villagers have given
 their lives in the process,

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:52.800
but we have to keep it safe,
 no matter what the cost.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.940
Even if that cost is your lives, huh?

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:03.430
Stop.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.320
Please wait right here.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:17.280
What?

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:26.030
You bastard!

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:29.300
You won't be going any farther.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.670
What?!

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.570
He's... strong!

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:39.260
What're you so scared for? 
We're just dealing with one guy.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:43.510
<i>I'll be able to handle demons of this 
level by myself without a problem.</i>

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:44.760
<i>However...</i>

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:48.160
<i>According to the villagers, 
there should be double the amount.</i>

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:49.400
It can't be!

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:53.980
Die!

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:55.330
Give us your salt!

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:02.070
Sorry I'm late.

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:10.990
You're late, you assholes.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.790
You're late, too!

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:16.160
Honestly... What were you all doing?

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.670
Well, I was having a smoke...

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:20.170
The food was really good!

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:21.790
I overslept.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.440
All of you, honestly...

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.560
Well, it's all right.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:30.310
You just barely made it in time.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.280
Looks like did get here 
just in the nick of time.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.380
I already took care of the ones over there.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:11.720
Aw...

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:17.360
The treasure's gonna dissolve away. 
Good work, Sanzo-sama.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:23.150
But it's nothing compared 
to that young man's life.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:39.500
Well, you exterminated the demons,
 but you ruined our precious salt. Deal's off.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:44.190
We're not giving you food or shelter. 
Hurry up and get out of our village.

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:45.030
But Mayor—

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.010
Shut up!

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:55.100
Hey.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:58.650
"I don't have a single 
cigarette to give—"

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:02.530
That's dangerous! The hell are 
you doing, you shitty priest?!

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.750
Quit dawdling and give me one.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.110
Sanzo.

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:06.610
Bastard!

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.190
You damn monkey, how dare you...

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:11.490
There's plenty to go around, so stop 
being stingy and give him one.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:26.150
You must be happy as well, Goku. 
You received quite a lot of buns.

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:30.000
Yeah! These are super tasty, so I'm happy.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.990
Honestly, we lucked out.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:35.900
Since the villagers were so 
kind to give us all of this,

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:39.030
we probably won't die from 
starvation for a while.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:43.040
The mayor was a jerk, but 
everyone else was super nice!

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:47.340
But we did almost end up working 
for free, thanks to Sanzo-sama.

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:49.040
Shut your mouth, you shitty water sprite.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:04.240
<i>We're treating this journey like we're just 
going around the corner to buy some smokes.</i>

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:40.150
<b>Episode 3
 "Sky Burial"</b>

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.890
Episode 3, "Sky Burial."

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:40.160
Watch without fail.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:43.150
<b>Ura Sai</b>

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:43.150
<b>Lettering: Hoshi Soichiro</b>

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.330
Ready, and...

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:43.150
Ura Sai!

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:51.480
What's so fun about this?

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:57.440
What are you doing here?!

00:21:57.440 --> 00:21:59.160
That's what I wanna know.

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:01.410
All right! Let's do this!

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:06.330
You swine!

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:10.310
Do you have any idea how rude it is to 
get in the bath with a bathing suit on?!

00:22:10.310 --> 00:22:11.600
That's what's bugging you?

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:14.710
Here I go! Woohoo!

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:17.240
Ow...

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:19.690
Oh... My bad.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:23.690
<b>Ura Sai</b>

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:23.690
<b>Lettering: Hoshi Soichiro</b>

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:20.900
Ready, and...

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:23.000
Ura Sai.

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:23.000
Ura Sai!

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:28.440
Good, good. Keep on going straight.

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:29.610
This way?

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:31.450
No, not that way.

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:32.090
Right here?!

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:33.880
No, no, no, no, no!

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:34.520
This way?

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:35.070
Yes, that—

00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:35.490
This way?

00:22:35.070 --> 00:22:37.240
No, no, no!

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:36.270
This way?

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:37.080
This way?

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:38.590
Would you calm down?

00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:37.950
This way?!

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:38.590
It's here, right?!

00:22:38.910 --> 00:22:39.920
Wait, no! That's—

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:44.370
Man, I can't seem to hit it.

00:22:44.370 --> 00:22:45.380
Gojyo, which way is it?

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:46.830
Which way...

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:50.260
Is he actually asleep?

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:53.600
<b>Ura Sai</b>

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:53.600
<b>Lettering: Hoshi Soichiro</b>

00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:51.940
Ready, and...

00:22:51.940 --> 00:22:53.610
Ura Sai...

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:03.860
So good!

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:05.000
I guess it's edible.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.920
Aren't you going to have any, Gojyo?
